      "content": "To define the parameters for a risk heat map, you can consider using a weighted scoring algorithm that incorporates various factors. A potential structure for the algorithm could include:\n\n1. Population density (30%): Average daily population density and population growth rate.\n2. Historical crime data (40%): Recent crime rates, crime patterns, and correlations with population density.\n3. Demographic volatility (20%): Measures of socioeconomic disparities, income inequality, and youth unemployment rates.\n4. Social media sentiment and community feedback (5%): Trends in social media posts and community feedback to gauge public sentiment.\n\nThis weighted structure can help balance the relative importance of each factor in predicting zones of potential social unrest. However, the specific weights and scoring mechanisms will need to be fine-tuned through pilot testing and evaluation.",
